+# Releasing
+
+Releases happen when the team agrees the main branch is ready, usually every
+second week after the planning meeting.
+
+1. Review the changelog top to bottom. Every entry must describe the change in
+   words a customer would understand.
+2. Bump the version in package.json.
+3. Tag the commit with the same version.
+4. Push the tag so the pipeline publishes the package.
+
+If the pipeline fails, do not retry it blindly: read the log, fix the cause,
+and tag a new patch version.
